From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NEXTBSD-RPI500: keep the early console past cninit (do not
 merge)

TEMPORARY bring-up instrumentation -- do not merge.

Measured on the board: the temporary locore markers show the kernel is
entered and reaches virtdone with the MMU on --

    Read kernel8.img bytes 15715704
    NVME off
    A          <- _start, MMU off
    B          <- page tables built
    C          <- virtdone, MMU on, socdev_va valid
    ...24s...
    reset

so the kernel runs. It just cannot be heard. cninit() selects the
console the FDT advertises, which on a Pi 500+ is RP1 UART0 behind
PCIe -- and with no bcm2712-pcie driver nothing can drive it. It then
unconditionally drops early_putc, and the kernel is mute from that
point on. On the wire that is identical to a kernel that died.

Keeping early_putc when SOCDEV_PA is defined routes cnputc() to the
PL011 the firmware left mapped, so the boot stays audible. Only
config/NEXTBSD-RPI500 defines SOCDEV_PA, so every other kernel keeps
stock behaviour.

Expected to expose a mountroot panic: this kernel has no root device.
That would be the phase-1 success condition, not a regression.
---
--- a/sys/kern/kern_cons.c
+++ b/sys/kern/kern_cons.c
@@ -212,11 +212,30 @@
 	cnselect(best_cn);
 
 #ifdef EARLY_PRINTF
+#ifdef SOCDEV_PA
 	/*
+	 * NEXTBSD-RPI500 bring-up (temporary): do NOT release the early
+	 * console.
+	 *
+	 * On the Raspberry Pi 500+ the console cninit() just selected is the
+	 * one the FDT advertises -- RP1 UART0, which lives behind PCIe. There
+	 * is no bcm2712-pcie driver yet, so nothing can actually drive it, and
+	 * dropping early_putc here makes the kernel silent from this point on.
+	 * That is indistinguishable on the wire from a kernel that died, which
+	 * is precisely the failure this is being used to diagnose.
+	 *
+	 * Keeping early_putc means cnputc() keeps writing to the PL011 the
+	 * firmware left mapped at SOCDEV_PA, so the boot is audible all the
+	 * way to mountroot. Guarded on SOCDEV_PA so only the board bring-up
+	 * kernel behaves this way.
+	 */
+#else
+	/*
 	 * Release early console.
 	 */
 	early_putc = NULL;
 #endif
+#endif
 	TSEXIT();
 }
 
